  "narrative_fragments": [
    "The river's surface quieted when they did, as if listening cost it nothing.",
    "At first light, a small hand counted fish twice and got two answers. The third time, she laughed and called the river a trickster.",
    "The fire spoke in quicker tongues when courage gathered, then settled with them.",
    "Wind changed its mind at the edge of their camp and went around, polite as a guest.",
    "After the rain, the earth drank with a low hush; small hands tucked seeds where the mud held sleep.",
    "They sifted the silt for root and tuber, and one bold lump turned out to be nothing but mud in the shape of hunger.",
    "Steam still threaded the air. She passed him the bone awl without looking; he caught it, turned, and used it to lift a stubborn thong from the wet hide.",
    "Rain needled the hide roof. Someone cupped a palm to catch drips and passed the water along like a sacred taste.",
    "Two hands reached for the same strip of dried meat. A third hand offered a thinner strip and said, solemn as a riverstone, that it was twice as filling because it was twice as thin.",
    "Na'da read the ground the way others read faces. When she pointed, the mother did not ask why; the way the wind moved agreed.",
    "At dawn, Na'da traced the missing print that explained the wrong turn. The mother nodded once — lesson kept, bond kept.",
    "Later, a man carried fire farther than asked and brought it back smaller, so sparks would not climb her hair. He said nothing. The night said the rest.",
    "A small grin cracked like bark; even hunger smirked a little.",
    "Hands worked in the same rhythm; threads remembered each other.",
    "A shoulder leaned and did not move away.",
    "They shared the last sweet root without counting.",
    "Eyes met, then stayed; the night felt shorter.",
    "Ropes held because voices did; knots learned their names.",
    "She carried the tired one without being asked; the ground felt kinder.",
    "Rain missed the fire once; they thanked the clumsy cloud."
  ],
